---
import AboutHeroImage from '../assets/placeholder-about.jpg';
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description="A gentle blog for mothers, written from lived experience of early motherhood."
	pubDate={new Date('2026-03-30')}
	heroImage={AboutHeroImage}
>
	<p>
		Hi — I'm a mother, and I started this blog because I needed it to exist.
	</p>

	<p>
		Early motherhood is beautiful and exhausting and confusing all at once. I found myself searching for honest, calm writing about sleep, feeding, emotions, and all the small daily chaos — and not always finding it. So I started writing it myself.
	</p>

	<p>
		<strong>Little by Little</strong> is for mothers of babies 0–2 years. It covers the things that actually matter in those early years: sleep patterns, postpartum recovery, feeding, child development, mental health, and finding balance when balance feels impossible.
	</p>

	<p>
		The tone here is warm, non-judgmental, and real. No perfect parenting advice — just honest writing from someone who's been there.
	</p>
</Layout>
